#: admin/help.php:61 admin/list.php:115
msgid "Duplicate"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:61
msgid "Creates a copy of the digest with the same forms, fields, and schedule. The copy starts active with no one-time date, so it is safe to edit before it sends."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:62 admin/list.php:120 includes/log.php:119
msgid "Send Now"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:62
msgid "Triggers the digest immediately using the current rolling window. This does not affect the next scheduled send - the schedule continues as normal. Useful for testing with real data or for sending on demand."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:63
msgid "Pause / Resume"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:63
msgid "Pausing cancels all scheduled cron events for that digest without deleting it. Resuming re-registers them. Use this instead of deleting when you want to temporarily stop sends."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:64 admin/list.php:130
msgid "Delete"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:64
msgid "Permanently removes the digest and cancels its cron events. This cannot be undone."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:69
msgid "Send log"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:71
msgid "\"Sent\" means the email was handed to your site's mailer (wp_mail). It does not guarantee delivery to the inbox - that depends on your hosting environment, DNS records (SPF/DKIM), and the recipient's spam filters."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:72
msgid "If a digest is not arriving, check these in order:"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:74
msgid "Spam or junk folder."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:75
msgid "A mail-logging plugin (e.g. WP Mail SMTP or Post SMTP) to see whether wp_mail even fired."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:76
msgid "Your host's mail logs or a transactional mail service (SendGrid, Mailgun, etc.) if one is configured."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:78
msgid "\"Skipped\" appears when a digest found no new entries and its \"When there are no new entries\" setting is set to skip. \"No entries\" means it sent a quiet-period notification instead."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:89
msgid "Digest & forms"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:91
msgid "The digest name is for your reference and doubles as the heading in the email when multiple forms are selected. It is optional - an untitled digest works fine if you only have one."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:92
msgid "When you select multiple forms, each form gets its own section and entry table inside the same email. Only forms that have entries in the time window produce a table - forms with no new entries are omitted silently."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:93
msgid "The \"Entries right now\" counter updates live as you tick and untick forms. It is a preview of what would be included if the digest ran at this moment, using your current field and form selections."
msgstr ""

